followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rdyro","id":12161222,"login":"rdyro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTYxMjIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12161222?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rdyro","id":12161222,"login":"rdyro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTYxMjIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Description\n\nDeserialization hangs indefinitely when `concurrent_gb` is smaller than the size of any single shard in the checkpoint. The call never returns and no error is raised.\n\nThis happens when using `GlobalAsyncCheckpointManager.deserialize(..., concurrent_gb=X)` where `X` is too small.\n\n---\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Save a checkpoint with at least one shard larger than `concurrent_gb`.\n2. Call `deserialize` with `concurrent_gb` set below that shard's size.\n3. The program hangs forever.\n\nExample scenario:\n\n- A shard is ~40 GB.\n- `concurrent_gb=32`.\n- Deserialization never begins.\n\n---\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- Deserialization should start normally, **or**\n- A clear error should be raised indicating that `concurrent_gb` is too small.\n\n---\n\n## Actual behavior\n\n- Deserialization waits indefinitely.\n- No shard starts loading.\n- No bytes are released.\n- No error is thrown.\n\n---\n\n## Root cause\n\nJAX's deserialization uses a byte-limit semaphore (`_LimitInFlightBytes`).  \nEach shard must reserve its *entire* size before reading. If:\n\nshard_size > concurrent_gb\n\nthen the reservation can never succeed. All tasks block waiting for “more free bytes,” but nothing ever runs to release any bytes. This causes a deadlock.\n\n---\n\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n- JAX version: 0.7.2\n- Platform: TPU\n- Distributed: no","closed_at":"2025-11-14T21:55:23Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12161222?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rdyro","id":12161222,"login":"rdyro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTYxMjIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/subscriptions","type":"U